 S~S  Release notes version 260123: simplesal repository activity: create the repository

------------------------------------------

  The metadata of the file system version control Application consisted of lines of text in
  a file edited by the developer.  This common method predates version control Application UIs.

  The information is included here to document the claim that SimpleSal was developed by TSC LLC.
    The file system version control database (some USB drives) contain a snapshot at each date.

  The software content described here is SimpleSal content written from scratch, from 2023/01/01.

      Date of
     Activity     Activity

  * 2023/05/25   Integrated the earliest time operations and operands with Arduino.
  * 2023/06/03   Completed working first pass of submenus, multi-input, console UI.
  * 2023/06/13   good working platform for menus and UI
  * 2023/06/17   math operations working: addition, assignment
  * 2023/06/23   math operations working: diff
  * 2023/06/30   math operations with multiple math operation contexts working (loop)
  * 2023/07/02   Math working well enough to test corners; all file banners made canonical.
  * 2023/07/09   Canonical format and structure for all include files, myUI and ssTEA.
  * 2023/07/11   Back to compiled and linked set of files after major refactor for Event API.
  * 2023/07/11   general-purpose functions used by ssTEA that User may also use.
  * 2023/07/18   significant refactoring/renaming/reordering as part of adding event complexities.
  * 2023/07/29   completed working first pass of Event Manager on the myUI side of event handling.
  * 2023/08/08   help, event api initialization   completed at the infrastructure level.
  * 2023/08/11   individual evapi commands under development; streamlining Ascii\* usage.
  * 2023/08/17   event API variables editable via "evapi" submenu.
  * 2023/08/20   first pass at API implementation, cleaned up types/values/return coherency.
  * 2023/08/23   end-to-end API call to drive the fsm for an event (allocation, FSMs, etc.)
  * 2023/09/01   Buildable and runnable, clean myUI/ssTEA nomenclature, APis, FSMs,  and operations.
  * 2023/09/05   Agency Api FSM and Agency Run FSM both operational as designed.  Event management.
  * 2023/09/11   event execution API and parameter type definitions closing the loop.
  * 2023/09/12   event execution occurs under control of Agency Root and Agency Next.
  * 2023/09/19   everything works for Agencying events except an accurate view of Time itself.
  * 2023/09/29   completed infrastructure of ssTEA management menus, canonical naming char pointers.
  * 2023/10/03   everything working except actually agency Root/Next; added ssTEA/myUI msg sets.
  * 2023/10/13   refactor for string placement optimization; through sheer luck: cT-/ssT-based Agency.
  * 2023/10/16   Time and Agency sputter to a new beginning on Arduino.
  * 2023/10/18   Time analysis and reporting from the inside.
  * 2023/10/23   Time and Agency under the control of ssTEA.
  * 2023/10/30   Time analysis working, which implies Time tracking is working as intended.
  * 2023/11/15   myUI interface to ssTEA FSMs more complete, ssTEA only lacking agency based on Time.
  * 2023/11/23   First end-to-end Agency API and Run FSM to define an event and AND THEN Agency it!
  * 2023/12/03   Agencying functional for single and recurring events; message choices prototyped.
  * 2024/01/03   Time and Data Events running as one-time or recurring events under software control.
